  "term": "abstract idea",
  "definition": "An abstract idea is a mental grasp of the shared qualities or attributes of something, considered on their own rather than as they appear in many separate examples. It goes beyond a general idea by setting aside the different instances and focusing only on the common character, such as thinking of humanity rather than particular people.",
